# The agent every candidate has to beat. One path, last non-comment line.
#
# `tools/fetch_fields.sh` copies this into every field it builds, as
# `champion.py`, and `tools/tournament.py` warns when a panel or round robin
# does not contain it.
#
# It points at `benchmarks/strongest.py` -- a plan recorded from the team at #1
# on the ladder, which also happens to win 92.4% of 1,920 episodes against the
# ten strongest plans mined here. It is committed precisely so this pointer
# resolves in a fresh clone.
#
# Read that 92.4% narrowly. `docs/ROADMAP.md` §10.5 checked local win% against
# the source teams' real ladder ratings across 100 mined plans and found no
# correlation (spearman -0.05, n=100); one team's own episodes span 14%-93%
# locally. A local win means a plan survives an unfamiliar board, not that it
# is a good strategy. The credential that survives scrutiny is where it came
# from.
#
# As of 2026-08-13 this is also what is on the ladder
# (`submissions/2026-08-13-topline/`), which was not true before: the previous
# champion `w39` topped a 477,225-episode round robin and came from the team at
# #358, while the plans from #6, #13 and #34 ranked below it.
#
# Update it when something wins on two independent fields -- and until §10.5's
# open item is closed, "two independent fields" here means one local and one
# external, not two local ones. Say so in docs/RUNS.md.
benchmarks/strongest.py
